## Programme rules
| Rule | Value |
|---|---|
| Number of audits planned | 25 audits, 134 auditor hours |
| Split by half-year | 19 audits in the first half-year (January to June), 6 in the second |
| Split by site | GDY-1: 10, HAM-2: 6, RTM-3: 5, GOT-4: 2, KLJ-5: 2 |
| Independence | an auditor never audits an area for which he or she is responsible |
| Moving a planned date | up to 30 days without approval; more than 30 days only with written approval by the Quality & Compliance Manager recorded on form KC-QF-170 (new rule after F-05 of the 2024 surveillance audit) |
| Audit report | issued within 10 working days of the closing meeting |
| Auditee response | corrective action plan within 15 working days of the report |
| Follow-up verification | within 60 days of the agreed completion date |
| External audit 2025 | Aldermark surveillance audit SA1 of the new certificate cycle, provisionally 22 to 24 September 2025 |
| Approved by | Benedikta Aaltonen, 2024-11-27 |
